#N canvas 40 60 1280 1000 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 10\ \ \ Spiking\ neurons\ \ -\ \ rhythms\ and\ pitches\ from\ spikes\ (1907\ /\ 2003) 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 970 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 970 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 970 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 Real neurons talk with SPIKES: short all-or-nothing pulses. What matters is when and how often they fire. Slow firing is a rhythm \, fast firing is a pitch. Here every spike rings a resonant filter., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 610 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 LEAKY INTEGRATE-AND-FIRE (Lapicque 1907 \, the oldest neuron model): the membrane is a leaky capacitor. Its voltage v creeps towards the input current I and leaks back. When v reaches 1 the neuron fires and v is reset to 0:, f 52;
#X text 30 203 v = v + (I - v) * dt / tau, f 52;
#X text 20 224 With a constant input it fires regularly \, at f = 1 / (tau * ln(I / (I - 1))) \, and never if I < 1 - a RATE CODE: a stronger input means faster firing., f 52;
#X text 20 290 IZHIKEVICH (2003): two equations \, seven famous firing patterns - regular \, bursting \, chattering ... (see the help of [nn.izh~])., f 52;
#X text 20 341 A SYNAPSE turns spikes into current: each spike adds a pulse that dies away (here [rpole~] \, a leaky integrator of about 5 ms). The LIF neuron can drive the Izhikevich neuron through it: two neurons talking., f 52;
#X text 20 422 MUSIC: a spike is a trigger. Below about 20 spikes per second you hear a rhythm \, above it a tone. The original NeuralNetwork patch pinged [bob~] filters the same way., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 430 430 empty empty LEAKY\ INTEGRATE-AND-FIRE 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 430 140 hsl 160 15 0 3 0 1 empty l10-I input\ current\ I\ (fires\ above\ 1) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 8000 1;
#X floatatom 598 139 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 430 180 hsl 160 15 2 200 1 1 empty l10-tau membrane\ tau\ (ms) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 8000 1;
#X floatatom 598 179 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 430 220 hsl 160 15 0.05 10 1 1 empty empty LFO\ on\ the\ current:\ rate\ (Hz) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 4200 1;
#X floatatom 598 219 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 430 260 hsl 160 15 0 1 0 1 empty l10-lfo LFO\ depth 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 0 1;
#X floatatom 598 259 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
